flowchart TD
    EV[Workflow event in a service] --> NOTE[pushNotification - in-app]
    NOTE --> BELL[Header bell + Notification center]
    BELL --> LINK[User follows link to the record]
    EV --> FE{fireEvent - automation}
    FE --> DUP{Already sent for this record?}
    DUP -->|Yes| SKIP1[Skipped - duplicate]
    DUP -->|No| ON{Automation switched on?}
    ON -->|No| SKIP2[History: SKIPPED - Automation is switched off]
    ON -->|Yes| RULE{Enabled rule for the event?}
    RULE -->|No| SKIP3[History: SKIPPED - No enabled rule]
    RULE -->|Yes| REC[Resolve recipients: Customer contact / Order salesman / Operations team / Document owner]
    REC --> CH{Channel}
    CH -->|Email or Both| EM[Render email template with variables]
    CH -->|WhatsApp or Both| WA[Render WhatsApp template]
    EM --> MODE1{Email mode}
    MODE1 -->|Demo| ED[QUEUED_DEMO then SENT_DEMO - not sent]
    MODE1 -->|Gateway| EG[POST /email/send - SENT = accepted by SMTP]
    WA --> MODE2{WhatsApp provider}
    MODE2 -->|Mock| WD[Sent - demo]
    MODE2 -->|Gateway| WG[OpenWA send-text - 201 = handed to WhatsApp]
    ED --> HIS[(Notification history)]
    EG --> HIS
    WD --> HIS
    WG --> HIS
    MAN[User composes manually] --> EM2["Compose email /communication/email/compose"]
    MAN --> WA2["Compose WhatsApp /communication/whatsapp/compose"]
    EM2 --> MODE1
    WA2 --> MODE2
    CALL["Log a call /communication/calls/create"] --> FU{Follow-up needed?}
    FU -->|Yes| FU1[Schedule follow-up - Call Follow-ups list: overdue / today / upcoming]
    FU1 --> FU2[Complete follow-up]
    FU -->|No| CLOSE[Call logged]
    CALL --> ORD[Link order to call]
